{"duration_api_ms":170610,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e300eafa-2c0f-4d88-bc21-4c6cb4989c2a","total_cost_usd":1.0553763999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":50,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52214,"cache_read_input_tokens":1707322,"output_tokens":14800,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1929},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52214,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":84178,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":374},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":50,"outputTokens":14800,"cacheReadInputTokens":1707322,"cacheCreationInputTokens":52214,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0553763999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1929,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":52214,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":25,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"PKT-0146 is finished and committed (`02ba3d2`). The round 3 verdict for docservice is **refactor, still in JavaScript**. All five acceptance commands pass, `theseus scope-check` reports no files outside the target, and `theseus validate` has 0 errors (its 4 warnings are about other packets and files).\n\n**The main finding is a speed regression from round 1.** I re-ran the original-vs-new comparison on synchronous conversions: the installed server on :80 against this worktree's DocService on :8099 (results in `.theseus/oracle/rounds/docservice-r3.md`).\n- The round 1 change makes the server check for the result at 50, 150, 350, 750, 1550 ms, doubling the wait each time up to 1 s (`converterservice.js:160-169`).\n- A conversion that ends between about 0.75 and 1.0 s is therefore answered at about 1.55 s. The old code, which checked once a second, answered at about 1.0 s.\n- Measured: pptx→pdf went from 1006 ms (old) to 1572 and 1610 ms (new). xlsx→pdf switches between 775 and 1565 ms from one run to the next.\n- Round 2 counted pptx→pdf as a gain only because the old server's first runs were still warming up.\n- Fast conversions still gain about 0.85 s (docx→odt 1016 → 164 ms).\n\n**What round 2 delivered:**\n- The storage fallback fix (PKT-0113) and the upstream fix 81132, for a client aborting mid-download (PKT-0114), are both correct. Neither saves any time users would notice.\n- Its two investigation packets, PKT-0115 and PKT-0116, are still pending, even though the factory planned this round as if every round 2 packet had run.\n\n**Round 3 plan**, ordered by how much time each step costs the user:\n- **P1:** break down the 538 ms DocService spends opening a document in the 10-page open journey. The other open journeys show only 81–206 ms for the same step. This is the only docservice step listed in `covers`.\n- **P2:** cap the wait between checks at 200 ms. That removes up to 0.8 s on conversions of 0.75–1.0 s, at the cost of at most 5 extra database reads per second on long conversions. PKT-0116 is meant to measure that cost.\n- The biggest docservice step, the 5 s wait before saving (85 % of save time), is not in the plan: PKT-0140 already covers it. Every other docservice step is in `not_covered` with a reason (each is under 4 % of its journey).\n\n**Decisions and other notes:**\n- I did not re-plan PKT-0115 or PKT-0116.\n- `DIAG-docservice-b.md` did not exist, so there was nothing to `git rm`.\n- `theseus validate` accepted plain step names in `covers`, even though `queue` and `result` appear in more than one journey.\n- The unit tests failed one test on one of three runs; it did not happen again on rerun.\n- No command was refused.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas** (recorded in the packet): a doubling wait capped at the old fixed interval can answer later than the fixed interval did. When comparing, include conversions that finish just after a check point, and make sure the original server is warmed up first.","ttft_ms":2981,"type":"result","duration_ms":333987,"uuid":"359c44aa-d07b-42eb-b267-2ee810f16406","ttft_stream_ms":1768,"time_to_request_ms":386,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":284,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":15,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":83,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":127,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":212,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":241,"process_anon_mib_result":151,"process_peak_rss_mib":246,"process_cpu_ms_turn":4546,"process_wall_ms_turn":333986,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1539,"process_wall_ms_streaming":113862,"main_stream_count":25,"main_stream_event_count":2141,"main_stream_chunk_count":1590,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":1539,"wall_ms":113862,"entries":25},"tool":{"cpu_ms":1444,"wall_ms":162439,"entries":24},"first_event_wait":{"